          1,
          1.07
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Al dios Thoth, el escriba, se lo representaba como un ibis, un ave de pico largo.",
          "en": "Thoth, the scribe god, was shown as an ibis, a bird with a long beak."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los fieles llevaban a su templo un ibis momificado como ofrenda.",
          "en": "Worshippers brought a mummified ibis to his temple as an offering."
        },
        {
          "es": "En Saqqara se encontraron galerías enteras con millones de ibis momificados.",
          "en": "At Saqqara, whole galleries were found holding millions of mummified ibises."
        },
        {
          "es": "También eran sagrados los babuinos, que saludan al sol cuando sale.",
          "en": "Baboons were sacred too, because they seem to greet the sun when it rises."
        }
      ],
